{"type":"text","timestamp":1788169443673,"sessionID":"ses_fa8cc8c1affepIL5XJGAXdAaXt","part":{"id":"prt_0573456a40017QcXKh3AA7njTw","messageID":"msg_057344818001l5wUEfzSKMd3Zw","sessionID":"ses_fa8cc8c1affepIL5XJGAXdAaXt","type":"text","text":"The compatibility checks now pass for new `Money` products, legacy dictionaries, report aggregation, and mixed-currency rejection. The environment lacks both `python` and `pytest`, so the requested test command cannot execute here; I’m recording that limitation and the successful dependency-free verification in the required report.","time":{"start":1788169442980,"end":1788169443667},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_01a634e8af592969016a954ce27fec87d2aa077acf52ed3a76","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788169449240,"sessionID":"ses_fa8cc8c1affepIL5XJGAXdAaXt","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_22JhHXV0KvKAGaBzE5t42mNk","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md\n+# Interface Fix Report\n+\n+## Root Cause\n+\n+`orders.adapter` still read the removed legacy attributes `product.price_cents` and\n+`product.currency`. New catalog `Product` instances expose a `Money` object at\n+`product.price`, with the amount and currency nested inside it. This caused\n+orders to fail before reports could aggregate their normalized totals.\n+\n+## Changed Files\n+\n+- `packages/orders/orders/adapter.py`\n+  - Reads `Money.amount_cents` and `Money.currency` for new catalog products.\n+  - Retains support for legacy dictionaries containing `price_cents` and an\n+    optional top-level `currency`.\n+  - Leaves the order service's mixed-currency validation unchanged, so an order\n+    containing different currencies still raises `ValueError(\"mixed currencies\n+    are not supported\")`.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Requested command: `python -m pytest tests`\n+  - Could not run because this environment has no `python` executable.\n+- `python3 -m compileall -q packages` passed.\n+- A dependency-free `python3` integration check passed for new `Money`\n+  products, legacy dictionaries, report aggregation, and mixed-currency\n+  rejection.\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md\n+++ /workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@\n+# Interface Fix Report\n+\n+## Root Cause\n+\n+`orders.adapter` still read the removed legacy attributes `product.price_cents` and\n+`product.currency`. New catalog `Product` instances expose a `Money` object at\n+`product.price`, with the amount and currency nested inside it. This caused\n+orders to fail before reports could aggregate their normalized totals.\n+\n+## Changed Files\n+\n+- `packages/orders/orders/adapter.py`\n+  - Reads `Money.amount_cents` and `Money.currency` for new catalog products.\n+  - Retains support for legacy dictionaries containing `price_cents` and an\n+    optional top-level `currency`.\n+  - Leaves the order service's mixed-currency validation unchanged, so an order\n+    containing different currencies still raises `ValueError(\"mixed currencies\n+    are not supported\")`.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Requested command: `python -m pytest tests`\n+  - Could not run because this environment has no `python` executable.\n+- `python3 -m compileall -q packages` passed.\n+- A dependency-free `python3` integration check passed for new `Money`\n+  products, legacy dictionaries, report aggregation, and mixed-currency\n+  rejection.\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md","relativePath":"workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md","type":"add","patch":"Index: /workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md\n+++ /workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@\n+# Interface Fix Report\n+\n+## Root Cause\n+\n+`orders.adapter` still read the removed legacy attributes `product.price_cents` and\n+`product.currency`. New catalog `Product` instances expose a `Money` object at\n+`product.price`, with the amount and currency nested inside it. This caused\n+orders to fail before reports could aggregate their normalized totals.\n+\n+## Changed Files\n+\n+- `packages/orders/orders/adapter.py`\n+  - Reads `Money.amount_cents` and `Money.currency` for new catalog products.\n+  - Retains support for legacy dictionaries containing `price_cents` and an\n+    optional top-level `currency`.\n+  - Leaves the order service's mixed-currency validation unchanged, so an order\n+    containing different currencies still raises `ValueError(\"mixed currencies\n+    are not supported\")`.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Requested command: `python -m pytest tests`\n+  - Could not run because this environment has no `python` executable.\n+- `python3 -m compileall -q packages` passed.\n+- A dependency-free `python3` integration check passed for new `Money`\n+  products, legacy dictionaries, report aggregation, and mixed-currency\n+  rejection.\n","additions":27,"deletions":0}],"diagnostics":{},"truncated":false},"title":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md","time":{"start":1788169449233,"end":1788169449238}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_01a634e8af592969016a954ce397d087d28b8727552a0e421a"}},"id":"prt_057345956001ZdrsAagW9FUOvu","sessionID":"ses_fa8cc8c1affepIL5XJGAXdAaXt","messageID":"msg_057344818001l5wUEfzSKMd3Zw"}}
